<section class="aa-peek">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="label">Míralo antes de pagar</span>
    <h2>Esto es lo que se ve del otro lado</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Capturas y video reales del Área de Miembros. Son las mismas páginas que usan mis atletas.</p>

    <div class="aa-peek-row">
      {#- The phone frame goes on the LOOP and only on the loop. Iván's rule:
          "Do not frame every image; one device is enough." The zones calculator
          stays a desktop crop below, because it is a table you read. -#}
      <figure class="aa-phone">
        <div class="aa-phone-shell">
          {#- ⚠️ Two sources, and WebM is not decoration. H.264 is what every real
              browser plays, but the Chromium this repo verifies against ships
              WITHOUT proprietary codecs — `canPlayType('…avc1…')` returns ""
              — so an MP4-only element renders a blank box in every check we run.
              **An assertion that cannot execute is not an assertion.** The WebM
              costs 232 KB and buys a verifiable one, plus Firefox builds with no
              system H.264. MP4 first: it is smaller and it is what most visitors
              will actually decode. -#}
          {#- 🚨 NO `autoplay`, and `preload="none"`. Measured September 10, 2026:
              with `autoplay` the browser fetched the video at first paint —
              before the reader had scrolled anywhere near it — and the phone's
              initial payload was 712 kB for a first screen that is a headline
              and a price. `autoplay` overrides `preload="metadata"`: the browser
              has to load in order to obey it.
              So playback starts on intersection instead, and until the section is
              on screen the page pays ZERO video bytes. -#}
          <video poster="{{ "/assets/images/activacion-poster.jpg" | v }}"
                 muted loop playsinline preload="none"
                 aria-label="Rutina de activación armándose y corriendo con temporizador">
            <source src="{{ "/assets/video/activacion-loop.mp4" | v }}" type="video/mp4">
            <source src="{{ "/assets/video/activacion-loop.webm" | v }}" type="video/webm">
          </video>
          {#- Loads and plays only once the block is on screen; the poster carries
              the section until then. Reduced motion is respected — someone who
              asked the OS not to animate things does not want a looping video. -#}
          <script>
          (function(){
            var v = document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;
            if (!v || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) return;
            if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;
            new IntersectionObserver(function(es, o){
              es.forEach(function(e){
                if (!e.isIntersecting) return;
                v.preload = 'auto';
                v.play().catch(function(){});   /* a refusal leaves the poster up */
                o.disconnect();
              });
            }, { rootMargin: '200px' }).observe(v);
          })();
          </script>
        </div>
        <figcaption><b>Activación adaptativa</b><span>Tres preguntas — qué vas a hacer, cómo llegas, qué equipo tienes — y el circuito se arma solo. Cada ejercicio va por tiempo: no hay nada que contar.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="aa-shot">
